  "findings": [
    "The complete B-only summand has last-child multiplier (etaMinus−t(Y))/2. The A-and-B summand has additional-gate multiplier (t(Y)−u(X0))/2, with the literal duplicate child already contributing 1. Y is the left endpoint of the actual last core child; X0 is the fixed core left endpoint. Both multiply the same full core summand.",
    "The exact two-row CutFiber sum follows sum_endingRows in its actual B-only/A-and-B order. Ring distributivity cancels the shared near/child value t(Y), leaving (etaMinus−u(X0))/2. Far data u remains arbitrary; the proof requires neither t=u nor a sign-square condition and cancels no exterior factor.",
    "nearFarTransform_ending uses the proved complete cut-fiber decomposition and all core cut sets. The multiplier depends only on the full collapsed interval, so finite-sum distributivity produces exactly the corresponding full core transform. The result imposes no supplied weight, child correspondence, solution or nonvanishing premise.",
    "The reversed-far theorem invokes tripleLift_neg to negate both H0 and t, producing (etaMinus+t(X0))/2 times the complete core transform with −H0 and unchanged b0. It does not change the ordinary array to the inverse for reversed far data; unary root terms remain present.",
    "The parent unit entry is zero because its left endpoint lies strictly before A and its right endpoint is B. The final ordinary equation uses the actual canonical inverse and its proved transform equation. If the collapsed interval has one leaf, end_unit_endpoint proves X0=cyclicPred s from strict endpoint arithmetic, so the etaMinus multiplier vanishes. Otherwise the core unit entry is zero.",
    "All actual ending intervals on the source domain are covered with arbitrary distinguished s, no n≥4 or geometric narrowing, and no sign/nonzero coefficient assumption. Unary compositions are included before splitting on the interval’s leaf count; the selected last boundary is never assumed to be the immediate predecessor in the general fiber identity."
  ],
  "limits": "This proves the complete formal ending transform, reversed-far formula and ending ordinary coordinate equation. Strict-spanning coordinates, final all-coordinate inverse identification, full physical-root specialization and the whole A-soft theorem remain separate. It asserts no equality of individual auxiliary and geometric open sums. This is same-model technical evidence only, with no source acceptance, canonical integration or stronger-model statement-fidelity approval."
